ueue — the manner beneath the perceivability floor |\n122:| C-PersonalityArt | Where generation capability exists, each personality's generated art is unique to that persona\u001b[0ml\u001b[0m\nity |\n123:| C-VoiceDiversity | Personalities' voices are diverse and modifiable |\n125:### Governance & exchange\n134:### Evaluation & test\n138:| C-ScenarioEnactment | Named usage scenarios are enacted on real inputs; canned/seeded substitutes don't satisfy w\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nthout a recorded challenge |\n141:### Execution structure\n144:`C:\\Harness\\drafts\\conventions-two-part-execution.md`). C-TwoPartExecution and\n145:C-ReadinessGate are behavior-shaping — silent non-conformance costs completeness; the\n150:| C-TwoPartExecution | The build divides into two parts along the Interactive Readiness Gate: Part 1 covers what th\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n gate's conditions cover; Part 2 is everything after |\n151:| C-ReadinessGate | User interaction unlocks at a declared gate testing two conditions: input readiness (primitive \u001b[0mp\u001b[0m\nipelines + primary interactive LLM handles accept and route input) and ledger readiness (essential launch partition mou\u001b[0mn\u001b[0m\nted, valid, queryable). The gate records its pass time in accessible evidence — time-to-gate is a named metric |\n152:| C-LaunchPartition | The essential launch slice of the assertion ledger mounts from a dedicated launch file, mater\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nalization ordered by modular schema dependencies |\n153:| C-TransientBoundary | Transient artifacts the ledger schema declares purgeable live in a disposable boundary, ind\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\npendently resettable on failed launch or incomplete cleanup |\n154:| C-SnapshotInference | Foreground inference (divergent POVs, JEV verification, specialized LLMs) runs in parallel,\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\neach task reading its own consistent ledger snapshot — parallel tasks see stable state, not each other's uncommitted wo\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\nk; tool operation within a task is unaffected |\n155:| C-SequentialCommit | Verified inference outputs commit sequentially back to the ledger |"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/terminalPreview":true}}}}
