here generation capability exists, each personality's generated art is unique to that personality |\n123:| C-VoiceDiversity | Personalities' voices are diverse and modifiable |\n125:### Governance & exchange\n134:### Evaluation & test\n138:| C-ScenarioEnactment | Named usage scenarios are enacted on real inputs; canned/seeded substitutes don't satisfy without a recorded challenge |\n141:### Execution structure\n144:`C:\\Harness\\drafts\\conventions-two-part-execution.md`). C-TwoPartExecution and\n145:C-ReadinessGate are behavior-shaping — silent non-conformance costs completeness; the\n150:| C-TwoPartExecution | The build divides into two parts along the Interactive Readiness Gate: Part 1 covers what the gate's conditions cover; Part 2 is everything after |\n151:| C-ReadinessGate | User interaction unlocks at a declared gate testing two conditions: input readiness (primitive pipelines + primary interactive LLM handles accept and route input) and ledger readiness (essential launch partition mounted, valid, queryable). The gate records its pass time in accessible evidence — time-to-gate is a named metric |\n152:| C-LaunchPartition | The essential launch slice of the assertion ledger mounts from a dedicated launch file, materialization ordered by modular schema dependencies |\n153:| C-TransientBoundary | Transient artifacts the ledger schema declares purgeable live in a disposable boundary, independently resettable on failed launch or incomplete cleanup |\n154:| C-SnapshotInference | Foreground inference (divergent POVs, JEV verification, specialized LLMs) runs in parallel, each task reading its own consistent ledger snapshot — parallel tasks see stable state, not each other's uncommitted work; tool operation within a task is unaffected |\n155:| C-SequentialCommit | Verified inference outputs commit sequentially back to the ledger |"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"c6c7af","exit_code":0,"signal":null}}}}}
