{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I've figured out the convention layer. Now I need to dive into the .002 codebase, which is about 690K lines across 20 Python modules and the UI. I'll focus on understanding specific components like `app/engines.py` for its fire-and-forget Popen calls, `app/speechfloor.py` for admission and playback logic, and `app/art.py` for seeded sigil art. I also need to examine `app/personas.py` and `app/seed.py` for preloaded personalities, `app/host.py`, `app/__main__.py`, and `launch.cmd` for launch and port handling, and `app/api.py` for its HTTP endpoints. The UI components in `app/ui/` require attention for the roster panel, color schemes, status bar, email commentary, conversation reset, and context display. Finally, I'll look into `scripts/scenarios.py` for driver bugs, `app/steward.py` for autonomous runs, `app/temporal.py` for date classification, and `app/needs.py` and `app/decision.py` for their respective functionalities."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:05:53.480372400+00:00"}}}}
