{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm deciding how to copy version .002 to .003. The baseline says copy everything, but runtime state is durable and specific to .002 runs. I'll copy the application code and documentation, but reset the runtime and evidence directories to ensure they are generated fresh by version .003. This avoids stale artifacts. I'll exclude runtime/, evidence/, launch-server.out, __pycache__, and .devin-surface.log. I'm also structuring the build execution into two parts: Part 1 will focus on the essential launch slice, including the ledger partition, input pipeline, primary LLM handle, and an interactive readiness gate that records input and ledger readiness pass times. Part 2 will cover all remaining components."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:05:54.527999+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-22T08:05:54.593269Z  INFO connect_post{path="/exa.product_analytics_pb.ProductAnalyticsService/BatchRecordAnalyticsEvents"}: connect_rpc::client: close time.busy=100µs time.idle=54.2ms
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the launch process. The essential launch slice of the assertion ledger will mount from a dedicated file, ordered by schema dependencies. This means a `runtime/launch.jsonl` will contain boot-time essentials like personas and tools, materialized first, followed by the rest of the ledger. Similarly, transient artifacts will reside in a resettable `runtime/transient/` directory."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:05:56.124750+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThere's a tension between parallel snapshot inference for divergent POVs and sequential commit for reacting to earlier contributions. If inference is parallel, personas can't react to each other's uncommitted work. A compromise: parallel inference on a snapshot of committed turns, sequential commit, and then an optional second stage for reactions. Or, simpler, parallel inference + sequential commit in floor order, and allow later personas' prompts to include earlier committed replies, but this breaks the \"own consistent snapshot\" rule."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:05:59.682008300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe core tension is between parallel inference on stable snapshots and sequential commit, which allows reactions. Since parallel inference inherently prevents same-turn reactions to uncommitted work, I'll adopt a design where inference runs in parallel on snapshots, and reactions are limited to deterministic acknowledgments generated at commit time. This will be noted in FEATURES.md."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:06:01.611555+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe G1 speech floor admission is currently broken because `engines.speak_local` spawns SAPI asynchronously without waiting for playback. To fix this, I'll rework `speechfloor.py` to use a playback worker thread that queues TTS requests, plays them synchronously, and only marks the floor as played after completion, ensuring sequential admission."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:06:05.333189300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm considering how to generate persona art. Since a ComfyUI or similar image generation backend is likely unavailable, I'll create parameterized SVG portraits. These will be vector-based, with traits driving features like face shape, hair, and color palette, stored as artifacts linked to personas and displayed with frames and subtle animations. I'll document this as generated vector art, not diffusion output."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:06:08.034009600+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-22T08:06:08.522440Z  INFO chisel_agent::skills_loading: skills discovery: cwd=C:\builds\project workspace_root=C:\builds additional_dirs=1 providers=[devin,agents_standard,cursor,windsurf,claude,opencode,zed,copilot,codex,kiro] scanned_scopes=3 loaded=48 by_provider=[builtin=3,cursor=7,devin=38] errors=0
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to ensure distinct personalities for the three preloaded agents, differentiating them through voice settings, speech patterns, interests, response templates, and system prompts. This persona-conditioned generation is crucial for both stub and Ollama modes. I've confirmed Ollama is live and running `llama3.2` in this environment."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:06:09.607278200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the G4 launch hygiene: before binding, I'll check if a port is already serving a Meridian instance and refuse with a clear error if it is, avoiding double-binding. To address the issue where closing a browser tab doesn't terminate the server, I'll implement a heartbeat watchdog using EventSource (SSE). SSE allows the server to detect client disconnects when the browser closes the tab, triggering a shutdown after a grace period. This approach is stdlib-friendly and handles background tabs effectively."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:06:12.916266300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to ensure the port binding logic correctly handles existing Meridian instances and other services. If another Meridian is already listening, I should exit with an error and evidence. If a non-Meridian service is using the port, the bind will fail anyway, so I'll report that failure honestly. I also need to check port 9760 for any lingering processes from a previous run."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:06:15.956485+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `connectors-F8-verify.json` file needs to be generated if it's claimed, and the current cycle will produce it. The `launch-server.out` file, currently generated by `.003`, might need renaming or fresh generation. The steward thread, which currently requires manual waking, should be made autonomous with a configurable interval, and its run count should be observable. A bug where temporal classification incorrectly treats 2030 as \"recent\" needs fixing by classifying dates relative to the actual current date. The \"S-focused-need\" mechanic requires deepening to allow conversational slot value supply and keep needs open until satisfied, with end-to-end demonstration. Finally, `S-chat-invocation` should be exercised by matching intents and need IDs to trigger chat responses."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:06:19.151583100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to verify FEATURES.md, evidence files, connector JSON, and runtime artifacts like SVGs. I'll also check the capability manifest for parity. This is a large task, so I'll copy the codebase, then explore key files like `host.py`, `engines.py`, and `speechfloor.py` before implementing fixes, building UI features, running tests, and updating the devlog. I also need to confirm the Python version and that the necessary services are running."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:06:21.712970600+00:00"}}}}
