{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the launch partition concept: it's a compacted subset of essential assertions (persona, tool, routing, decision, source, user-settings) written to `runtime/launch-partition.jsonl` on shutdown. On boot, the Ledger mounts this partition first, then loads the main journal, skipping duplicate assertions. Materialization is ordered by schema dependency: config/user-settings/source first, then tools, personas, and needs. The gate's readiness test now checks for the partition's existence and queryability."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:14.798403500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm moving transient artifacts like probes and scenarios into a new `runtime/transient/` directory. This directory will be independently resettable on failed launches or unclean shutdowns, using a boot marker to detect stale states. Additionally, I'm improving launch hygiene by pre-binding a port check in `__main__.main` to detect existing instances and setting `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` on Windows to prevent double-binds."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:17.363605700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the SSE endpoint's watchdog logic: it should only trigger a graceful shutdown if the connection count drops to zero for more than 12 seconds *after* at least one client has connected. This accounts for browser heartbeat reconnects, which happen around 3 seconds. I'll add a `--no-watchdog` flag for scenarios and probes that don't use SSE. I'm also adding a version stamp to the app and exposing it via `/api/version`. For G1 speech, I'll modify `speak_local` to optionally block until synthesis and playback complete, likely by running PowerShell's `Speak` command synchronously."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:20.812751200+00:00"}}}}
