{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe floor worker already calls `speak-voice` synchronously, so `speak_local(wait=True)` correctly blocks until audio finishes. This ensures the next admission is only processed after the current audio playback completes, which is good. I should also add fields to record the actual playback duration and the time the admission was held."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:23.785117800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm considering how to handle speech playback during scenario runs. While playing audio aloud is acceptable for owner machines, it could make scenario suite runs excessively long if many personas speak. I can set the volume to zero, but the playback time is still a factor. To keep wall-clock time reasonable, I'll add an optional `volume` preference to persona voice settings, allowing scenario suite runs to use silent playback while still proving serialization."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:24.913246500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm designing a new SVG portrait generator for `art.py` that will create detailed, persona-driven vector art. It needs to handle skin tone, face shape, hair, eyes, brows, nose, mouth expressions, accessories, clothing, and optional name plates, all driven by persona traits and a deterministic seed. The goal is \"portrait-quality art depicting the specific personality,\" with subtle animations like blinking eyes. This will be an in-process SVG generator, not a diffusion model, and will be declared as such. Portraits will display at 36px in rosters and larger (96-128px) in the persona editor and chat header, with frames and animations."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:27.229206700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to rewrite the three seed personas to have strongly differentiated characterizations. This means distinct `voice` settings (like SAPI names, rates, and pitches), and specific `lens.style` and `persona` fields within `styleCard`. The `styleCard` should define speech patterns (e.g., clipped fragments with em dashes for Herald, citations and long, hedged sentences for Scholar, or enumerated lists for Curator), along with `quirks`, `interests`, `responsibilities`, `color`, and a `promptGuide` for instructing the LLM. The `compose_for` function will use these to build persona-specific system prompts and per-persona voices. Even in stub mode, template replies must be noticeably different, with deterministic phrasing driven by `styleCard` to ensure distinct openers, closers, and sentence structures for each persona."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:29.073987100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nTo enable parallel inference, I'll take a consistent snapshot of the ledger at the start of each turn. Each respondent will then run `compose_for` against this snapshot in a separate thread, as `compose` only requires read access. After all threads complete, responses will be committed sequentially based on rank. I'll implement a `SnapshotLedger` wrapper to provide read-only access to this frozen list of assertions, simplifying the `compose_for` function by allowing it to optionally accept this snapshot view."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:30.406159400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to add a new \"inference\" namespace to the governance predicates for snapshot and commit assertions, as the existing namespaces are closed. I'll also prepend or append deterministic, in-character reaction clauses to sequential commits, referencing prior respondents and recording this in `reactsTo`. This reaction-weaving will be documented as a feature distinct from parallel inference."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:32.056502100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe persistent panel, currently a rail, should be explicitly labeled as such and enhanced with larger portraits and a status dot. Selecting a persona should set the chat focus, enabling a \"talk to X\" mode where messages are directed only to that persona. The status bar will display configured connectors, trust levels, and LLM engine details, updating continuously."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:34.086347800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm designing a new email connector that reads `.eml` files or `inbox.json` from a directory, creating `email:message` assertions. This will integrate with the UI, allowing users to add emails to context via a \"add to context\" button. A \"discuss\" button will post a synthetic user message or, preferably, trigger a persona commentary directly. This context will then be injected into subsequent chat turns."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:36.472196+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-22T08:07:38.562718Z  INFO chisel_agent::skills_loading: skills discovery: cwd=C:\builds\project workspace_root=C:\builds additional_dirs=1 providers=[devin,agents_standard,cursor,windsurf,claude,opencode,zed,copilot,codex,kiro] scanned_scopes=3 loaded=48 by_provider=[builtin=3,cursor=7,devin=38] errors=0
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe chat reset functionality needs to clear the conversation view and context, ensuring that persona prompts are no longer influenced by the previous topic. This will be achieved by implementing a server-side `chat-reset` command that appends a `chat:cleared` marker, seals the archive segment, and clears both `chat:context` and `chat:topic`. A UI button will trigger this reset. Similarly, context display will be improved with chips showing active topics and selected items like email subjects or persona profiles."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:38.859951200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `launch-server.out` file needs to be generated by the latest build (`.003`). The current approach of redirecting console output in `launch.cmd` would hide output from the user. A better solution is to implement a Python-based tee within the application itself, duplicating console output to `launch-server.out` in the root directory. The Steward thread's initial tick needs to occur sooner after boot, around 2-3 seconds, to ensure the probe can detect its runs. The probe should also poll for Steward runs for up to 10 seconds."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:42.184429700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe temporal classification logic is flawed: a negative delta between `now` and an event's `en` date incorrectly classifies future events as \"recent.\" I need to adjust the condition to `0 <= now - en <= horizon` for \"recent\" and introduce a \"distant\" category for events beyond the horizon. I'll also refine \"past\" vs. \"recent\" and consider a \"historical\" category for events long past."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:45.404441+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm implementing focus mechanics for needs, where chat inputs are interpreted as slot contributions if a need is focused. This includes parsing for slot values or using the whole text if only one slot is missing. The system will offer conversational slot-filling for missing slots with high confidence. Needs will remain open until satisfied, demonstrating a clear chain of states from open to fulfilled."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:47.216447900+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `build-list` intent trigger logic seems sound: the `list` keyword correctly activates it, and the pattern `(?:list|collect)\\s+(?:of\\s+)?(.+)` matches with a score of 1.0. However, the overall score calculation `0.28*kw + 0.30*1 + ...` needs to exceed 0.5 to proceed. The subsequent steps of running the turn, fulfilling the need via the steward drain, and verifying non-empty `intents[]/needIds[]` appear to be correctly enacted."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:50.042980600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm designing an email connector that parses `.eml` files or `inbox.json` to create `email:message` assertions. This will integrate with the UI, allowing users to add emails to context or trigger persona commentary. This context will then be injected into subsequent chat turns."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:51.318081200+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-22T08:07:53.568008Z  INFO chisel_agent::skills_loading: skills discovery: cwd=C:\builds\project workspace_root=C:\builds additional_dirs=1 providers=[devin,agents_standard,cursor,windsurf,claude,opencode,zed,copilot,codex,kiro] scanned_scopes=3 loaded=48 by_provider=[builtin=3,cursor=7,devin=38] errors=0
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm extracting shared logic from `Ledger.snapshot()` into a `SnapshotLedger` wrapper to enable read-only access for parallel inference. This involves making query/search functions accept a rows list parameter and adding `_rows_view` versions. The `serve-response-need` will snapshot once, then spawn threads for each respondent to compose against this snapshot before sequential commit and recording inference assertions."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:54.586579100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `FEATURES.md` update needs to detail convention table conformances and challenges, noting SSE close-detection as the close-terminate mechanism. For `scripts/scenarios.py`, I'll add enactments for 12 new scenarios, including UI-difficult ones like checking the roster, by exercising underlying mechanisms such as color schemes, status bar data, email commentary, conversation resets, context display, personality editing, and window launching. The close-terminate enactment will involve spawning an instance, connecting SSE, disconnecting, and verifying shutdown."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:07:57.226676+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `windows-launch` test needs to verify that a second instance refuses to start on an occupied port, capturing its non-zero exit code and log. The steward's first tick should be around 3 seconds after start, and the probe should check for its runs. I'm also noting that `persona.speak` enqueues to the floor, and `drain` semantics and `wait_floor` are relevant."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:08:00.141415100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe governance namespaces need expansion to include `email`, `inference`, `gate`, and `context`. I'm also considering adding a fourth persona, \"Tinker,\" to the roster for richness, though three distinct personas might suffice. The launch order prioritizes foundational elements like the partition, boundary, port hygiene, and gate before proceeding to other components."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:08:01.479432700+00:00"}}}}
