{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm refining the `host.py` context management. The \"transient boundary\" concept implies a purgeable directory, distinct from the main `runtime/` install state. I'm identifying what's truly transient: render cache, snapshot debug data, and the boot marker. These will go into `runtime/transient/`. The `gate.json` should persist in the root for evidence, not be purged. A `boot.marker` in the transient dir will signal an unclean shutdown, triggering a wipe of the transient contents upon restart. Clean shutdowns will remove this marker. I'm also adding a `Ledger` with a `launch-partition.jsonl` path. The `ctx.close()` method will now handle writing the partition, removing the boot marker, and stopping the floor."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:08:36.555933+00:00"}}}}
