{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I've found an issue with boot marker logic: `ctx.close()` isn't called on all shutdown paths, specifically watchdog shutdowns. I need to wire it into `__main__.py`'s finally block and the watchdog shutdown. I'm also updating `__main__.py` to include port ownership checks, exclusive binds, a gate, watchdog via SSE, and other features like versioning and transient reset notes. The port ownership check will use an HTTP GET request to `/api/version` to detect stale instances."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:08:46.098741700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the server shutdown sequence: `server.shutdown()` needs to be called from a separate thread, which the watchdog thread handles. After `serve_forever` returns, the main thread will execute `ctx.close()` and `steward.stop()`. I'll also record a `launch:shutdown` assertion. The boot log will be written to `<root>/launch-server.out`. I've clarified the gate timing, defining `started_ms` as the program start time and calculating time-to-gate from process start. The boot order is now: Ctx, builtins, seed packs, engine probe, gate, steward, and finally serve. The gate must pass before user interaction unlocks; if it fails, the launch will report honestly with a banner, and the HTTP surface will still serve for diagnostics, but the steward won't start."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:08:48.970712200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nFor ledger readiness, I check `partition_mounted > 0` OR `seed:loaded rows` OR `live > 0`. On first boot, `partition_mounted` is 0 because the file doesn't exist, but seeds are loaded, so `live > 0` passes. This logic seems correct. Now, I'm rewriting `__main__` to incorporate these checks."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:08:49.404669500+00:00"}}}}
