{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm adding SSE endpoints for events, context, emails, persona updates, chat resets, and gates. The `state()` function will also be updated to include gate, context, theme, and floor. I've subclassed `ThreadingHTTPServer` to create `MeridianServer`, ensuring exclusive address binding on Windows. For SSE, I'm using a queue per client, with the server tracking active clients and total SSE connections. The SSE handler sends events, pings clients if no data is available, and cleans up client queues when disconnected or the server shuts down."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:09:09.209686800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the SSE client management, deciding to use `srv.clients` as the primary set for active clients and `srv.sse_total` for the count, while making `srv.sse_clients` a property that returns the length of `srv.clients`. This simplifies the watchdog logic. The `BaseHTTPRequestHandler` needs to handle persistent connections and client disconnects gracefully within the SSE keep-alive loop. I've also outlined new API endpoints for version, events, gate status, email listings, context selection, chat resets, persona updates, and focus."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:09:11.951794900+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm extending the POST /api/chat endpoint to accept `personaId` and `focusNeedId`, and creating a POST /api/needs/<id>/focus endpoint to set the chat's focus. Chat context will be stored as an assertion with the subject \"chat\" and predicate \"chat:context\". When a focus need is set, I'll offer the input text as a candidate for missing slots in the focused need's tool template if no new intents are opened. Context will be injected into prompts as \"Active context the user selected: ...\". For email commentary, I'll use POST /api/context/select to assert `chat:context`, choose a respondent, and compose commentary referencing the email excerpt."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:09:14.242726400+00:00"}}}}
