{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm refining the `serve-response-need` function. It now selects respondents based on the input text, and can filter them by `personaId` if provided. Before parallel inference, I'm logging the snapshot used for ledger reads. The `compose_for` function will now accept this snapshot, ensuring consistency across parallel calls. I'm also adding error handling for the `work` function within the parallel inference block."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:09:39.104551200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm implementing sequential commits for chosen personas, ensuring each composition is valid before proceeding. I'll use a reaction clause, prepended to the text, to indicate a persona is building on a previous one. These clauses will be deterministic and persona-specific, with a default format like \"(reacting to {prev})\", and specific overrides for certain personas like Herald. I also need to ensure `compose_for` receives `extra_context` to include relevant chat context, like the currently selected item, in its prompt."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:09:42.136491300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nWhen conversational slots are missing, I'm now using the input text as a candidate and adding it to the needs list with a high confidence score. I'm also clarifying that the `select-context` tool should only set `chat:context` and not `chat:context-item` when handling email. For profiles, I'm setting the context but not generating commentary unless specifically required, as per the scenario."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:09:44.847364300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm adding `chat-reset` to clear chat state and `persona-update` to manage persona fields, extending its functionality to include `lens`, `voice`, and `color`. The `fn_run_chat_turn` will now accept a `personaId` and `focus`. For the email connector, I'll parse `.eml` files and JSON fixtures, automatically configuring the `inbox-local` connector on first boot if it's not already set up."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:09:47.287162800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm considering adding a fourth persona, \"Wickett,\" to enrich the roster beyond the current three. This would involve rewriting the personas in `getting-started.json` to include strong fields and styleCards, and I need to verify the personas within the seed study-vessel pack."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:09:47.697542500+00:00"}}}}
