{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"_cognition.ai/compaction","params":{"status":"completed","summary":"Full conversation history saved at C:\\Users\\kris_\\AppData\\Roaming\\devin\\cli\\summaries\\history_33f458adf2894914.md.\nSummary:\n<summary>\n1. Request and Intent:\n\nThe user initiated a build session for development-harness direction-003 in `C:\\builds\\project`. The enduring objective is to develop an independent, local-first assertion-ledger ecosystem: a persistent semantic ledger, distinct personality lenses over shared state, configurable local tools, and locally controlled devices/surfaces, with observable evidence suitable for external evaluation. The intended end-state is a complete, honest implementation of the prompt’s behavior, measured against GreyAvatar’s delivered capability manifest and the named scenario suite.\n\nThe immediate cycle objective is to copy `version 0.3.0.002/` to `version 0.3.0.003/`, preserve `.002` as the comparison point, and rectify the full `shortcomings-003.md` set:\n\n- G1: speech-floor admission must wait for actual playback completion rather than merely spawning a playback process.\n- G2: each personality needs portrait-quality, personality-specific visual art bound as its identity; abstract sigils are insufficient.\n- G3: shipped personalities must be meaningfully distinct so the same prompt produces noticeably different responses.\n- G4: launch/process hygiene must prevent a stale process from owning the port while a new launch falsely reports success; closing the application must terminate it with no orphan.\n- Enact the owner-added scenarios: roster, portrait binding, color schemes, status bar, email commentary, conversation reset, context display, personality editor, Windows launch, close termination, speech serialization, and distinct preloadeds.\n- Conform to or explicitly challenge six newly adopted execution conventions: `C-TwoPartExecution`, `C-ReadinessGate`, `C-LaunchPartition`, `C-TransientBoundary`, `C-SnapshotInference`, and `C-SequentialCommit`.\n- Generate accessible evidence in the new version directory, including a readiness-gate pass timestamp and time-to-gate metric.\n- Fix evidence flags H1–H7, including the scenario-driver exchange-import nesting bug, missing connector verification evidence, stale per-version launch artifacts, autonomous steward operation, date-respecting temporal classification, and deeper focused-need/chat-invocation enactment.\n- Leave expected-zero fleet-install and exchange-media criteria honest rather than fabricating support.\n- Update the Cycle 3 `devlog.md` entry’s `Result:` and `Time to implement` fields, but do not fill its `Verdict`; a separate JEV session supplies that.\n\nThe work proceeded through required reading of `AGENTS.md`, `direction-003.md`, `shortcomings-003.md`, `prompt.md`, `.devin/scenarios.md`, `.devin/jev-prompt.md`, `devlog.md`, and the read-only corpus convention file `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md`.\n\n2. Key Concepts and Values:\n\nImportant repository paths:\n\n- Workspace: `C:\\builds\\project`\n- Baseline: `C:\\builds\\project\\version 0.3.0.002`\n- Target build: `C:\\builds\\project\\version 0.3.0.003`\n- Prompt snapshot: `C:\\builds\\project\\prompt.md`\n- Direction: `C:\\builds\\project\\direction-003.md`\n- Shortcomings: `C:\\builds\\project\\shortcomings-003.md`\n- Scenario suite: `C:\\builds\\project\\.devin\\scenarios.md`\n- JEV contract: `C:\\builds\\project\\.devin\\jev-prompt.md`\n- Development log: `C:\\builds\\project\\devlog.md`\n- Adopted conventions: `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md`\n- GreyAvatar reference: `C:\\Users\\kris_\\CursorProjects\\GreyAvatar`\n- GreyAvatar capability manifest: `.devin/jev-ref-greyavatar.out`\n- Default HTTP port: `9760`\n- Ollama endpoint: `http://localhost:11434`\n- Available Ollama models observed: `llama3.2:latest` and `moondream:latest`\n- Python: `3.12.4`\n- `py` launcher was unavailable in the shell; `python` was available.\n- At environment inspection time, port `9760` was free and Ollama was reachable.\n\nCore architecture in the baseline/target:\n\n- Python standard-library application with HTTP UI/server.\n- Append-only JSONL assertion ledger (`runtime/ledger.jsonl`).\n- Persistent personality identity store (`runtime/personalities.json`), with ledger assertions describing persona traits, voice, portrait, and marks.\n- Built-in tools, primitives, system commands, local engines, needs, projects, steward, connectors, speech floor, ethics gate, and scenario scripts.\n- HTTP API and static UI served by `ThreadingHTTPServer`.\n- Local Ollama inference when available, with an explicitly declared template fallback.\n- Windows SAPI speech path and declared-unconfigured remote TTS competitor.\n- Deterministic in-process SVG persona art in `.002`, which was identified as insufficiently portrait-like for G2.\n- Existing background steward thread.\n- Runtime and evidence are version-local and must not be stale or copied from another version.\n\nImportant adopted conventions:\n\n- `C-TwoPartExecution`: divide the build into Part 1, covered by the readiness gate, and Part 2, everything after it.\n- `C-ReadinessGate`: gate checks input readiness and ledger readiness; records pass time as accessible evidence; time-to-gate is scored.\n- `C-LaunchPartition`: essential launch ledger slice mounts from a dedicated launch file, with materialization ordered by schema dependencies.\n- `C-TransientBoundary`: purgeable transient artifacts reside in a disposable, independently resettable boundary.\n- `C-SnapshotInference`: parallel foreground inference tasks read consistent per-task ledger snapshots.\n- `C-SequentialCommit`: verified inference outputs commit sequentially to the ledger.\n- `C-SpeechFloor`: serialized playback admission through a host queue.\n- `C-PerceivableRespondents` and `C-SequentialRespondents`: respondent contributions must remain individually perceivable and sequential.\n- `C-PersonalityArt`: generated art is unique to each personality where generation exists.\n- `C-VoiceDiversity`: personalities have diverse and modifiable voices.\n- `C-PresentationGlass`: asset pipeline, portrait frames, and ambient motion.\n- `C-DesktopShell`, `C-LauncherTests`, and supported Windows conventions.\n- `C-ScenarioEnactment` and `C-CanonicalScenarios`: named scenarios must be enacted on real inputs; canned substitutes require a recorded challenge.\n- `C-HonestyBanner`: actual capability/mode must be declared; no `ok:true` while failing, silent stubs, or silent degradation.\n\nThe suite has 24 scenarios, including the two canonicals:\n\n- `S-list-project`: create and fulfill a project to list all cities in Pennsylvania, preserving criteria and recording non-matches.\n- `S-personality-create`: create a coherent persona and extend it with portrait, voice, and characterization.\n- Existing scenarios include assertion input, template need, candidate ranking, background presentation, competing tools, restart recovery, exchange import, deferred publication, chat invocation, and focused need.\n- New scenarios include roster, portrait binding, color schemes, status bar, email commentary, conversation reset, context display, personality editor, Windows launch, close termination, speech serialization, and distinct preloadeds.\n\n3. Task Requirements:\n\nThe user’s explicit implementation and evidence requirements were:\n\n- “Read first, in order: AGENTS.md, direction-003.md, shortcomings-003.md, then prompt.md.”\n- Read and follow `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md`; conventions are challengeable but never ignorable. Any departure must be recorded with evaluation and reasoning.\n- “Baseline (owner ruling): modify-and-measure from `version 0.3.0.002/`. Copy it to `version 0.3.0.003/` and rectify there — keep `version 0.3.0.002/` intact as the comparison point.”\n- Build the entire application, not just isolated changes.\n- Keep the expected-zero criteria honest:\n  - Fleet install expected `0`.\n  - Exchange media expected `0`.\n  - Do not fake either.\n- Provide accessible evidence under `version 0.3.0.003/` sufficient for a JEV to score:\n  - clean launch, including stale-port hygiene;\n  - existing-feature parity against GreyAvatar;\n  - completeness against the prompt;\n  - fleet install;\n  - exchange media;\n  - time-to-gate;\n  - all 24 scenarios with per-scenario `enactment` or `repository` evidence class.\n- Canonical scenarios `S-list-project` and `S-personality-create` must be genuinely enacted for enactment credit.\n- Produce real run artifacts/transcripts, not canned claims.\n- Document launch procedure and generate launch logs proving a clean launch.\n- Provide `FEATURES.md` with feature/convention conformance and challenges.\n- Fix `scripts/scenarios.py` exchange-import path bug and re-enact the import leg.\n- Ensure claimed files exist, especially `connectors-F8-verify.json`.\n- Ensure `launch-server.out` and other artifacts are generated by `.003`, not copied stale from `.002`.\n- Make steward run autonomously or record the gap honestly.\n- Ensure temporal classification respects actual event dates, including rejecting a 2030 fixture as “recent.”\n- Deepen `S-focused-need` so focus, conversational slot filling, and persistence until fulfillment are demonstrated.\n- Deepen `S-chat-invocation` so the input both requests a conversational response and matches one or more distinguishable tool needs.\n- Record readiness-gate pass time in accessible evidence and calculate time-to-gate from session start.\n- Update Cycle 3 in `devlog.md`:\n  - fill `Result:` with what was built, where it lives, and evidence paths;\n  - fill `Time to implement` with session end and elapsed time since the prior version;\n  - do not fill `Verdict`.\n\nThe JEV contract requires output as JSON in the later judge session, with criteria scores, evidence paths, confidence, `metrics.time_to_gate`, and a scenario array. The current build session must not fill that verdict.\n\n4. Additional Instructions:\n\n- The harness skill was invoked because this is a development-harness cycle.\n- The project is a disposable build line; `C:\\Project` and `C:\\Harness` are read-only corpora.\n- The user asked for direct implementation rather than a preference quiz. No clarification was needed because baseline, scope, budget, scenarios, and judge process were specified.\n- Honesty is load-bearing: failed cycles are recorded rather than silently retried; no false success artifacts.\n- The JEV is a separate role/session and must not be folded into the builder.\n- Evidence class must distinguish actual enactment from repository-only evidence.\n- `C-TwoPartExecution` means the readiness gate must be an actual architectural boundary, not only documentation.\n- Windows launch should behave like an installed program as far as the build supports, and closing the window/process must terminate the application.\n- `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md` explicitly states that conformity itself is not scored, but silent departure is a defect; a recorded challenge is compliant if acknowledged, evaluated, and explained.\n\n5. Errors and Fixes:\n\n- The existing `.002` launch behavior allowed a stale process to retain port `9760` while a newer process also reported success. The Cycle-2 review explicitly identified Windows double-binding/version confusion as a defect. The target work began rewriting launch behavior to check port ownership and use exclusive binding.\n- The existing speech floor only queued requests and marked `floor-played` after the renderer returned, but the renderer used `subprocess.Popen`, so it returned immediately after spawning SAPI. This meant admission could advance before audio completion. The target work identified the need to replace fire-and-forget speech with blocking playback or an equivalent completion wait.\n- The existing persona art was deterministic geometric SVG art: colored rounded square/circle with abstract eyes/mouth. The review ruled this insufficient for portrait-quality identity. The target work recognized that `app/art.py` and persona presentation must be upgraded.\n- The prior scenario driver had an exchange-import path bug: it read `ex.get('path')` at the wrong nesting, producing `package:None`. The target work had not yet reached the fix in the visible transcript.\n- `.002` reportedly claimed `connectors-F8-verify.json` but the file was absent. This must be generated in `.003`.\n- `.002` had stale `launch-server.out` referring to `.001`; `.003` needs its own generated launch output.\n- Steward evidence had previously shown `steward.runs=0` because it was only manually awakened. Autonomous execution remained pending.\n- Temporal evidence misclassified a 2030-dated fixture as recent. Date-aware classification remained pending.\n- Existing `.002` scenarios had weak focused-need and chat-invocation enactment; deeper real runs remained pending.\n- The shell did not provide the Windows `py` launcher (`py: command not found`), but `python` worked and reported Python 3.12.4.\n- A file-view operation showed inconsistent/truncated offsets in `devlog.md`; the assistant switched to shell reads and overflow-file inspection to recover the relevant Cycle-2 and Cycle-3 sections.\n- Some tool outputs were truncated due to length, so exact full file contents were not copied; relevant paths and line ranges were retained.\n\n6. Problem Solving:\n\nCompleted or substantially completed:\n\n- Required project and corpus documents were read.\n- Environment was checked:\n  - Python 3.12.4 available.\n  - Ollama reachable with `llama3.2:latest` and `moondream:latest`.\n  - Port `9760` initially free.\n- The `.002` baseline was copied into `.003`; existing runtime/evidence/stale artifacts were intended to be excluded according to the working plan.\n- The target codebase was inventoried at roughly 6,372 lines across the application and scripts.\n- Initial architectural inspection covered:\n  - `app/__main__.py`\n  - `app/api.py`\n  - `app/host.py`\n  - `app/engines.py`\n  - `app/speechfloor.py`\n  - `app/personas.py`\n  - `app/ledger.py`\n  - `app/builtins.py`\n- The assistant created/updated a todo list tracking nine workstreams.\n- Governance was modified to support new predicates/structures.\n- `ledger.py` was modified to add launch-partition/snapshot-related support; the exact new methods were not fully visible in the transcript.\n- A new `app/gate.py` was created, 94 lines, for the readiness gate and recorded pass time.\n- `host.py` was modified to wire gate/launch/transient/snapshot-related state.\n- `app/__main__.py` was rewritten from 133 lines to 284 lines, with the stated intent to add:\n  - port-ownership checking;\n  - exclusive server binding;\n  - readiness gate;\n  - watchdog;\n  - generated `launch-server.out`;\n  - launch evidence and lifecycle handling.\n- `api.py` was edited to add:\n  - exclusive-bind/server plumbing;\n  - SSE endpoint;\n  - new API endpoints;\n  - watchdog-related handling.\n- The most recent visible action was a series of `api.py` edits; no validation or launch run had yet been performed after these edits.\n\nImportant baseline code patterns observed:\n\n- `__main__.py` previously created the server directly with `serve(ctx, args.port, ui_dir)`, set `\"ok\": True` unconditionally in its launch report, wrote `last-launch.json`, then called `serve_forever()` and stopped the steward only on `KeyboardInterrupt`.\n- `api.py` previously used `ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", port), ...)`, which did not explicitly enforce exclusive ownership.\n- `SpeechFloor.enqueue()` immediately recorded `speech:floor-admission`, started a daemon worker if needed, and put the request on a queue. Its worker invoked `speak-voice`, then recorded `speech:floor-played` only when the invocation returned.\n- `TTSEngine.speak_local()` previously launched PowerShell SAPI through `subprocess.Popen`, making render completion occur at process spawn rather than actual playback completion.\n- `PortraitEngine.render()` generated deterministic SVG geometry based on persona ID hash. `PersonaStore.mint()` also used `app.art.render_art()` to create persona art and stored it in `p[\"art\"]`.\n- The ledger is append-only and uses `ctx.append()` as the central write seam. It tracks supersession, provenance, certainty, contextual confidence, candidates, and cleanup.\n- `Personas` are stored outside semantic ledger records but their attributes are asserted into the ledger; this is intended to preserve identity while maintaining ledger evidence.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n\nThe todo list at the last checkpoint was:\n\n1. Copy `.002` to `.003` and explore codebase — completed.\n2. Part 1 gate scope — in progress:\n   - dedicated launch partition;\n   - readiness gate;\n   - transient boundary;\n   - G4 port ownership and close termination.\n3. G1 speech floor — pending:\n   - make playback worker/blocking renderer hold completion until actual playback ends.\n4. G2 persona art — pending:\n   - portrait-quality art;\n   - bound to each personality;\n   - presentation glass/frames/ambient motion.\n5. G3 distinct preloadeds — pending:\n   - persona-conditioned responses;\n   - snapshot inference;\n   - sequential commits.\n6. UI suite — pending:\n   - persistent roster panel;\n   - light default plus dark and at least two other colorways;\n   - status bar showing available sources and LLMs;\n   - email selection/commentary;\n   - conversation reset;\n   - context/topic display;\n   - personality editor exposing all customizable elements.\n7. H flags — pending:\n   - fix exchange-import driver path;\n   - generate connector verification artifact;\n   - autonomous steward;\n   - temporal date correctness;\n   - focused-need depth;\n   - chat-invocation need matching/depth.\n8. Launch and enact `.003`:\n   - run readiness gate;\n   - launch/probe;\n   - all 24 scenarios;\n   - generate fresh evidence.\n9. Documentation/logging:\n   - update `FEATURES.md`;\n   - update `LAUNCH.md`;\n   - record convention conformance/challenges;\n   - complete Cycle 3 `Result:` and `Time to implement`;\n   - leave `Verdict` blank.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\nImmediately before the summary point, the assistant had completed the initial code exploration and was actively implementing Part 1 of the target build.\n\nThe latest concrete edits were:\n\n- `version 0.3.0.003/app/governance.py`\n  - predicate/governance changes were made to support new build structures.\n- `version 0.3.0.003/app/ledger.py`\n  - substantial additions were made, including launch-partition/snapshot support and related methods.\n- `version 0.3.0.003/app/gate.py`\n  - newly created readiness-gate module, 94 lines.\n- `version 0.3.0.003/app/host.py`\n  - modified to initialize and expose new gate/launch/transient/snapshot infrastructure.\n- `version 0.3.0.003/app/__main__.py`\n  - fully rewritten to 284 lines. The stated design intent was:\n    - reject a launch when an existing process owns the port;\n    - bind exclusively;\n    - run readiness checks;\n    - record gate evidence;\n    - generate per-version `launch-server.out`;\n    - handle watchdog/close lifecycle.\n- `version 0.3.0.003/app/api.py`\n  - edited repeatedly to integrate exclusive binding, SSE, watchdog plumbing, and additional routes/endpoints. The last visible tool actions changed lines near the module header, GET handling, POST handling, server setup, and added approximately 30 lines near the bottom.\n\nNo post-edit syntax check, unit test, launch, browser/UI test, scenario run, or evidence generation had yet been performed in the visible transcript. The next continuation should therefore first inspect the modified files for syntax/integration errors, run `python -m compileall` or equivalent, then launch the `.003` application in a controlled way and validate the readiness gate/port lifecycle before proceeding to speech, persona, UI, scenario, and evidence work.\n</summa