{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm rethinking `speak_local`. It seems the `Popen` approach was causing issues because it didn't wait for playback to finish. Switching to `subprocess.run` should fix this, as it's synchronous and will block until PowerShell exits. This also means the worker will genuinely wait for the speech to complete. I'll add a `wait` parameter, defaulting to `True`, to control this blocking behavior."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:11:31.841202300+00:00"}}}}
