{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call","toolCallId":"exec:0#448b596b1aa846f3b250b7c083269c9c","title":"Ran mkdir, ls","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"cd \"C:\\builds\\project\\version 0.3.0.003\" && mkdir -p fixtures/inbox && cat > fixtures/inbox/001-marta.eml << 'EOF'\nFrom: Marta Ellison <marta@harborline.example>\nTo: you@localhost\nSubject: Reunion roster — headcount needed by Friday\nDate: Tue, 18 Nov 2025 09:14:00 -0800\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\"utf-8\"\n\nHi —\n\nFinal call on the Harbor reunion roster. I need a definite headcount\nby Friday or the hall goes to the wedding party. So far I have 14\nconfirmed, 6 maybe. Which are you?\n\nAlso: someone still has the lighthouse slides from '98. If it's you,\nbring them.\n\n— Marta\nEOF\ncat > fixtures/inbox/002-bank.eml << 'EOF'\nFrom: Harborline Credit Union <alerts@harborline.example>\nTo: you@localhost\nSubject: Statement ready: November 2025\nDate: Mon, 24 Nov 2025 06:02:00 -0800\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\"utf-8\"\n\nYour November statement is ready.\n\nChecking ****4471:  $4,182.56\nSavings  ****2290:  $11,908.10\n\nNo action required. This mailbox is unmonitored.\nEOF\ncat > fixtures/inbox/003-devon.eml << 'EOF'\nFrom: Devon Aoki <devon@fieldnotes.example>\nTo: you@localhost\nSubject: Field notes: the Otter Creek survey\nDate: Wed, 26 Nov 2025 17:45:00 -0800\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\"utf-8\"\n\nAttached the raw transect counts from Tuesday. Two anomalies worth\na second look:\n\n 1. Station 4 — heron count tripled vs last year (9 vs 3). Either a\n    new rookery upstream or a double-count. I'd bet on the rookery.\n 2. Station 7 — turbidity reading looks instrument-flawed; the probe\n    was fouled with duckweed.\n\nWeather held. Boots did not.\n\n— D\nEOF\nls fixtures/inbox/","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"cd \"C:\\builds\\project\\version 0.3.0.003\" && mkdir -p fixtures/inbox && cat > fixtures/inbox/001-marta.eml << 'EOF'\nFrom: Marta Ellison <marta@harborline.example>\nTo: you@localhost\nSubject: Reunion roster — headcount needed by Friday\nDate: Tue, 18 Nov 2025 09:14:00 -0800\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\"utf-8\"\n\nHi —\n\nFinal call on the Harbor reunion roster. I need a definite headcount\nby Friday or the hall goes to the wedding party. So far I have 14\nconfirmed, 6 maybe. Which are you?\n\nAlso: someone still has the lighthouse slides from '98. If it's you,\nbring them.\n\n— Marta\nEOF\ncat > fixtures/inbox/002-bank.eml << 'EOF'\nFrom: Harborline Credit Union <alerts@harborline.example>\nTo: you@localhost\nSubject: Statement ready: November 2025\nDate: Mon, 24 Nov 2025 06:02:00 -0800\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\"utf-8\"\n\nYour November statement is ready.\n\nChecking ****4471:  $4,182.56\nSavings  ****2290:  $11,908.10\n\nNo action required. This mailbox is unmonitored.\nEOF\ncat > fixtures/inbox/003-devon.eml << 'EOF'\nFrom: Devon Aoki <devon@fieldnotes.example>\nTo: you@localhost\nSubject: Field notes: the Otter Creek survey\nDate: Wed, 26 Nov 2025 17:45:00 -0800\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=\"utf-8\"\n\nAttached the raw transect counts from Tuesday. Two anomalies worth\na second look:\n\n 1. Station 4 — heron count tripled vs last year (9 vs 3). Either a\n    new rookery upstream or a double-count. I'd bet on the rookery.\n 2. Station 7 — turbidity reading looks instrument-flawed; the probe\n    was fouled with duckweed.\n\nWeather held. Boots did not.\n\n— D\nEOF\nls fixtures/inbox/"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["mkdir","ls"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:13:42.871920200+00:00"}}}}
