{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#792b4c8c4138492b8f5e2e24a6c47a17","status":"in_progress","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"# Scenario suite — project line of development\n\nPer-scenario evaluation criteria for JEV verdicts and owner review. Each scenario scores\n0–1 on the implementation's **ability to enact** it. Suite is evolvable at review points\n(rubric revision 2026-11-19: scenario suite added alongside `completeness`).\n\n## Scoring conventions\n\n- **Evidence class:** `enactment` (the build ran or its run artifacts/transcripts/logs\n  demonstrate the scenario — strongest) or `repository` (mechanism confirmed present and\n  plausibly enactable — weaker; used for reference builds assessed without launch).\n  Record the class per scenario; do not pretend repository evidence is enactment.\n- **Score the outcome, not just the mechanism.** A scenario fails if the machinery exists\n  but the produced result is wrong, incoherent, or violates the scenario's stated bar.\n- Sources: `prompt.md` §Observable demonstrations (D1–D11); the UX reference scenarios in\n  `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\InstructionsForUserExperience.txt`; owner canonical tests\n  (marked **canonical**).\n\n## Suite\n\n| ID | Scenario | Exercises | Source |\n|----|----------|-----------|--------|\n| S-assertion-input | Typed or spoken user input recorded as a source-aware assertion with provenance | assertion ledge\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\n, attribution | D1 |\n| S-template-need | Template governing an unfulfilled requirement created and filled from explicit or incidental tool w\u001b[0mo\u001b[0m\nrk | unmet-need floor, templates, slots | D2 |\n| S-candidate-ranking | Candidate values ranked by contextual confidence and recency; failed evidence retained | confid\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\nnce model, supersession | D3 |\n| S-list-project | **Canonical.** Create and fulfill a project to *list all the cities in Pennsylvania* | template mode\u001b[0ml\u001b[0m\n, projects, iterative list completion, criteria preservation | D4, D11; UX iterative list completion |\n| S-personality-create | **Canonical.** Create a minimal personality from a minimal input and extend it through later p\u001b[0mo\u001b[0m\nrtrait, voice, and characterization work into a coherent persona | persistent identity, generated needs, characterizati\u001b[0mo\u001b[0m\nn coherence | D5; UX createAvatar |\n| S-background-present | Completed background work presented as a relevant result through a distinct personality, prese\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\nving ledger evidence | stewardship, attention, personality presentation | D6; UX research-to-conversation |\n| S-competing-tools | Locally competing tools expressing the same need produce comparable results | tool ontology, inde\u001b[0mp\u001b[0m\nendent realizations | D7 |\n| S-restart-recovery | Useful state recovered after restart; records consolidated without losing provenance | durabilit\u001b[0my\u001b[0m\n, recovery, cleanup | D8 |\n| S-exchange-import | Storefront/exchange package imported, contents held below the threshold for action or acceptance \u001b[0m|\u001b[0m\n exchange schema, sub-threshold import | D9 |\n| S-defer-publication | Unconfigured nonlocal publication request refused or deferred, request and status recorded | au\u001b[0mt\u001b[0m\nhority boundary, graceful deferral | D10 |\n| S-chat-invocation | Chat input requests a conversational response while matching one or more tool needs; each need re\u001b[0mm\u001b[0m\nains distinguishable | chat-turn chain, conversational tool matching | UX chat tool invocation |\n| S-focused-need | Unmet need moved into focus; values supplied conversationally; need remains available until its requ\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nrement is fulfilled | focus/context mechanics, conversational slot-filling | UX focused unmet need |\n| S-personality-roster | Selectable roster of personalities presented as a persistent panel, conventionally the left co\u001b[0ml\u001b[0m\numn | roster surface, personality switching | owner 2026-11-22; cf. C-InspectionSurfaces |\n| S-portrait-bind | Creating a personality produces portrait-quality art depicting that specific personality, bound to \u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nt as visual identity | portrait generation, art-to-persona binding | owner 2026-11-22; C-PersonalityArt, C-Presentation\u001b[0mG\u001b[0m\nlass |\n| S-color-schemes | Theme selector offers dark mode plus at least two other colorways; fresh launch opens in light mode\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\n| theming | owner 2026-11-22 |\n| S-status-bar | Status bar continuously shows available sources and LLMs | capability surfacing | owner 2026-11-22; cf\u001b[0m.\u001b[0m\n C-HonestyBanner, C-MultiSourceAccess |"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/terminalPreview":true}}}}
