rsonalities presented as a persistent panel, conventionally the left co\u001b[0ml\u001b[0m\numn | roster surface, personality switching | owner 2026-11-22; cf. C-InspectionSurfaces |\n| S-portrait-bind | Creating a personality produces portrait-quality art depicting that specific personality, bound to \u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nt as visual identity | portrait generation, art-to-persona binding | owner 2026-11-22; C-PersonalityArt, C-Presentation\u001b[0mG\u001b[0m\nlass |\n| S-color-schemes | Theme selector offers dark mode plus at least two other colorways; fresh launch opens in light mode\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\n| theming | owner 2026-11-22 |\n| S-status-bar | Status bar continuously shows available sources and LLMs | capability surfacing | owner 2026-11-22; cf\u001b[0m.\u001b[0m\n C-HonestyBanner, C-MultiSourceAccess |\n| S-email-commentary | User selects a received email from a list and adds it to conversational context; the active pers\u001b[0mo\u001b[0m\nnality offers commentary on it | source ingestion, context injection, persona commentary | owner 2026-11-22; cf. C-Conf\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nguredAccounts |\n| S-conversation-reset | Reset button clears the conversation when it has moved to a different topic, keeping personali\u001b[0mt\u001b[0m\ny prompts on-topic | topic segmentation, prompt hygiene | owner 2026-11-22; C-ConversationArchive |\n| S-context-display | Active conversational topic/context displayed when the user selects a profile, email, or other re\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\nult | context surfacing | owner 2026-11-22; C-ConversationArchive |\n| S-personality-editor | Editor tab exposing all customizable personality elements for editing | persona editing surfac\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n | owner 2026-11-22 |\n| S-windows-launch | Application launches from MS Windows like an installed program | packaging, launch | owner 2026-11\u001b[0m-\u001b[0m\n22; C-SupportedOS-*, C-LauncherTests |\n| S-close-terminate | Closing the application window terminates the program — no orphaned process | process lifecycle |\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nowner 2026-11-22; C-DesktopShell |\n| S-speech-serialization | Generated speech waits until the previous speaker finishes rather than overlapping | speech \u001b[0mf\u001b[0m\nloor, sequential respondents | owner 2026-11-22; C-SpeechFloor, C-PerceivableRespondents, C-SequentialRespondents |\n| S-distinct-preloadeds | Shipped personalities differ enough in persona and style that the same prompt elicits noticea\u001b[0mb\u001b[0m\nly different responses | persona distinctness | owner 2026-11-22; C-VoiceDiversity |\n\n## Scenario notes\n\n- **S-list-project:** no exact answer exists, but there is a huge variety of bad answers\n  (townships or CDPs passed off as cities, tiny subsets, invented names, duplicates,\n  criteria reset on refinement). Score the delivered list's defensibility — real\n  incorporated municipalities, breadth, preserved criteria — plus non-matches recorded as\n  results-that-do-not-match for review, per D4.\n- **S-personality-create:** good coverage of many parts working together — identity\n  assignment, portrait/voice/characterization needs generated, and the resulting persona\n  coherent and distinct. Score coherence of the whole, not the parts' existence.\n- **Owner additions 2026-11-22:** the twelve scenarios below S-focused-need exercise UI\n  and shell capabilities. Where one overlaps a convention (noted `cf. C-*` / `C-*`), the\n  convention mechanism governs: a build may depart with a recorded challenge — conformity\n  direction is not scored, only reckoning on the record (owner ruling 3, 2026-11-19).\n1122:def fn_import_exchange(ctx, inp, grant):\n1167:def fn_export_exchange(ctx, inp, grant):"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/terminalPreview":true}}}}
