{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm realizing that `_index` needs to deduplicate by ID, as partition rows were also persisted to `ledger.jsonl` and share IDs. The fix is to skip indexing if an ID is already present. Also, `_mount_partition` should only count newly indexed rows, not all mounted ones, and the stats after remounting should match the on-disk count. Handling `superseded` rows also deduplicates correctly. A subtle point is that if a partition row is mounted first and then the same row is loaded from the ledger, deduplication by ID prevents a double entry, so the order of rows doesn't really matter."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:15:48.021399600+00:00"}}}}
