{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#d13cc5f9262342d0b97dd31ec448d80e","status":"in_progress","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"@echo off\nREM Meridian launcher — documented procedure in LAUNCH.md\ncd /d \"%~dp0\"\npython -m app --port 9760 --open\n# FEATURES.md — Meridian (version 0.3.0.002) capability manifest\n\n**Direction-002 build.** Rectifies the shortcomings-002 set (F1–F8) on top of\nthe 0.3.0.001 baseline. New machinery this cycle: `app/ethics.py`,\n`app/speechfloor.py`, `app/art.py`, `app/temporal.py`, `app/connectors.py`,\n`app/compare.py`, `app/setbuild.py`, `app/archive.py`. Enactment evidence:\n`evidence/scenarios/*.json` (real run transcripts) + `runtime/artifacts/`.\n\nClassification: **parity** = functional coverage of a feature GreyAvatar\ndelivers; **new** = capability beyond the reference (incl. rectified\nshortcomings); **absent** = not implemented (declared, not faked).\n\nReference: `C:\\Users\\kris_\\CursorProjects\\GreyAvatar`. This build is a fresh\nPython-stdlib implementation — no code ported; architecture re-derived from\n`prompt.md`.\n\n## Truth model\n\n| Capability | Class | Where |"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/terminalPreview":true}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#d13cc5f9262342d0b97dd31ec448d80e","status":"in_progress","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"@echo off\nREM Meridian launcher — documented procedure in LAUNCH.md\ncd /d \"%~dp0\"\npython -m app --port 9760 --open\n# FEATURES.md — Meridian (version 0.3.0.002) capability manifest\n\n**Direction-002 build.** Rectifies the shortcomings-002 set (F1–F8) on top of\nthe 0.3.0.001 baseline. New machinery this cycle: `app/ethics.py`,\n`app/speechfloor.py`, `app/art.py`, `app/temporal.py`, `app/connectors.py`,\n`app/compare.py`, `app/setbuild.py`, `app/archive.py`. Enactment evidence:\n`evidence/scenarios/*.json` (real run transcripts) + `runtime/artifacts/`.\n\nClassification: **parity** = functional coverage of a feature GreyAvatar\ndelivers; **new** = capability beyond the reference (incl. rectified\nshortcomings); **absent** = not implemented (declared, not faked).\n\nReference: `C:\\Users\\kris_\\CursorProjects\\GreyAvatar`. This build is a fresh\nPython-stdlib implementation — no code ported; architecture re-derived from\n`prompt.md`.\n\n## Truth model\n\n| Capability | Class | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| Append-only assertion ledger, durable JSONL, restart reload | parity | `app/ledger.py` |\n| Typed values (`string/number/boolean/enum/ref/list/map`), closed claimant vocabulary, governed predicate namespaces |\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nparity | `app/model.py`, `app/governance.py` |\n| Computed views (`render_view`): supersession + trust resolution at read time; no second store | parity | `ledger.rend\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\nr_view` |\n| Source-bounded confidence: effective = min(certainty, context, source ceiling); recency breaks ties | parity | `ledge\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\n.effective_confidence` |\n| Basis kinds: captured-input / interpretation / source-evidence / generated / execution / user-choice / durable-result\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\n/ import / refusal | parity | `model.BASIS_KINDS` |\n| Candidate slots inspectable with source + confidence until a tool selects | parity | `ledger.candidates_for`, `needs.\u001b[0mc\u001b[0m\nandidates` |\n| Contextual confidence (applicability) carried separately from certainty | parity | `Assertion.context` |\n\n## Components & needs\n\n| Capability | Class | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| Component ontology: tool (data) / system-command (`object.verb`) / primitive (closed allow-list) | parity | `app/tool\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\n.py`, `app/builtins.py` |\n| Tool-logic-as-data: closed-op interpreter (`set/query/search/view/candidates/append/appendEach/when/invoke/invokeEach\u001b[0m/\u001b[0m\nengine/emit/repeat/result/fail`), no eval | parity | `app/dsl.py` |\n| Single write seam `ledger.append`; other stores via system commands | parity | `ctx.append`, `COMMANDS` |\n| Unmet needs (`need:*`): open floor, gate eval, defer/cancel/supersede/fulfill, `need.fulfill` command | parity | `app\u001b[0m/\u001b[0m\nneeds.py`, `tools.fulfill_need` |\n| Templates: required/optional slots, `minCertainty`, grant requirement | parity | `spec.template`, `tools.evaluate_gat\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n` |\n| Consumable, scoped, witnessed, lockable grants; ungranted consequential request = recorded deferral | parity | `tools\u001b[0m.\u001b[0m\nissue_grant`…, demo 10 |\n| Deferred work: missing slots leave need open with `need:deferred`; refinement via related assertions | parity | `need\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\n.defer_need`, `needs.refine_need` |\n| **Competing-tool lifecycle (F3): general `compare-run` machinery — every tool expressing a `need:` is invoked on the \u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\name input, results normalized to a shared understanding, ranked; each `comparison:row`/`comparison:run` recorded; outco\u001b[0mm\u001b[0m\nes feed trust churn** | **new (F3)** | `app/compare.py` |\n| Genuinely competing retrieval tools: `retrieve-set-wiki-table` vs `retrieve-set-wiki-category` (both `set.members`, d\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nfferent live strategies, comparable members) + `render-speech-sapi` vs `render-speech-remote` (`speech.render`) | **new\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\n(F3)** | `app/setbuild.py`, speech tools |\n| **Bounded decision model for routing/evaluation — fixed feature vector, weighted sum, weights as ledger config, `deci\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\nion:score`/`decision:respondent` traces, O(#tools×7) per decision** | **new (A9)** | `app/decision.py` |\n| **Tool-trust churn: inadequate/failed results lower a bounded rank multiplier [0.1–1.0] among alternatives without ma\u001b[0mk\u001b[0m\ning the tool ineligible; successes recover it** | **new (A5 / D-ToolTrustChurn)** | `decision.record_outcome`, demo 7 |\n| **Novice tool authoring: `validate-tool` (errors + warnings + repair hints), `create-tool`/`edit-tool`/`inspect-tool`\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nwith telemetry view** | **new (A10)** | `fn_validate_tool`, Workshops tab |\n| 68 registered components at launch (30+ tools, 12 commands, 12 primitives) | parity-scale | registry manifest, probe |\n\n## Personalities\n\n| Capability | Class | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| Persistent persona identities outside the ledger (`runtime/personalities.json`); `persona:*` assertions as ledger vie\u001b[0mw\u001b[0m\n | parity | `app/personas.py` |\n| Mint/edit persona; **unique generated art per persona** — motif family from interests, palette from identity, ambient\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nSVG motion, portrait frame, artifact + `persona:art` assertion (C-PersonalityArt / C-PresentationGlass) | **new (F7)** \u001b[0m|\u001b[0m\n `app/art.py`, `fn_generate_portrait` |\n| **Ethics gate (F1): every mint passes liveness research through the wikipedia connector + maxim:objection patterns; v\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\nrdicts allowed / mark-required / admonish-required / refused; gate cards + `ethics:gate` rows; refusals recorded (`pers\u001b[0mo\u001b[0m\nna:mint-refused`, basis refusal)** | **new (F1)** | `app/ethics.py`, `personas.mint`