{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm exploring how to handle needs with missing required slots, like `arm-countdown` needing minutes. Focusing the need via API and then conversationally filling the slot seems like a good pattern. `set-response-depth` with its \"value\" slot is a clear example: the chat fills \"3,\" fulfilling the need and setting the depth. I'll also check the roster, portrait binding, color schemes, status bar, and email commentary tests."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:16:05.411262100+00:00"}}}}
