{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm reviewing the `fn_run_chat_turn` logic. It seems the `supersedes` calculation is inefficient, querying the ledger twice. I can simplify this by ensuring the query result is stored and then checked for emptiness before accessing the last element's ID. This avoids a potential `AttributeError` and redundant calls."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:17:37.777522300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nWait, there's a subtlety: `open_needs` shows a \"tool-request\" kind for our need. `needs.defer_need` sets the status to deferred, which means `st[\"status\"] != \"open\"` in `fn_focus_need` returns an error \"need X is deferred\"! Focusing on a deferred need fails. I need to handle this: focusing should be allowed on open OR deferred needs. I'll check `needs.need_state` statuses to see if `defer_need` changes the status or just adds a flag."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:17:38.598281200+00:00"}}}}
