{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"It looks like `fulfill_need` correctly defers when the gate isn't ready, and `evaluate_gate` handles candidates from `needs.candidates` even without `minCertainty`. The focused fill in `fn_run_chat_turn` happens after intents are parsed, which seems fine. `persona.speak` also routes correctly, and `wait_floor` should handle serial speech playback. `fn_focus_need` works as expected for deferred needs."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:17:44.854882700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm tracing the context selection and persona updates. `fn_select_context` handles `kind=\"need\"` correctly, even if `item_id` is `None`. The `/api/context/select` endpoint correctly invokes `select-context` with the request body. For persona updates, `fn_persona_update` uses fields like \"lens\" and \"voice\" to update `ctx.personas`, and then re-renders art based on these changes. The `/api/personas` mint endpoint also seems to correctly read the \"lens\" from the input body. I've also noted that `ctx.ledger.partition_mounted` exists in `gate.py` and that `host.py` passes `partition_path` to `Ledger` during `Ctx` initialization."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:17:46.500488300+00:00"}}}}
