{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"The second boot attempt should exit quickly due to port refusal, but the total time is much longer than expected. I suspect `read_all` on the second process might be waiting too long, or the refused instance isn't exiting as it should. The port check logic seems correct, so the issue might be with how `read_all` interacts with the process exit."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:22:18.764578900+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nIt seems the SSE connection closing isn't the cause of the early exit. The `p1` server, still running on the expected port, is being connected to instead of `p3`. This leads `p1`'s watchdog to time out and shut down, but the check incorrectly attributes `p3`'s premature exit (due to port refusal) to this shutdown sequence, masking the real issue."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:22:20.983534300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"similar-snowdrop","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to fix launch-check to stop p1 before step 3, but it's still running. It might be stuck at `read_all(p2)` or `p3`'s `wait_up` returning quickly, then SSE connect, sse.close(), and `p3.poll()` already being non-None. The portFreed check fails because `get(\"/api/honesty\")` succeeds while p1 is still serving, and then `p3.terminate()` is called on an already dead process. This should have finished, unless `sse.close()` doesn't free server-side promptly."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:22:22.979945100+00:00"}}}}
